From: CBOC-Vita <cboc-vita@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] 1.3: a scene that does not load its depth/stencil surface begins with the background mask set, and the full-target mask quad is left out (vglSetMaskBackground, MASK_BG)

MSC_VGX_VGL_MASKBG (the Galaxy port's MASK_KEEP of its patch 0018, on by default on its console since r84, and its patch 0022 for the display's scene; written again from the description):
with the RT depth hint a scene need not load its depth/stencil surface and then starts from the background mask (clear); with the scissor test off update_scissor_test drew a
quad over the whole target to set the mask everywhere (patch 0026's records only help a scene that loads and stores). The background mask is part of the surface the scene is
begun with, so vgl_mb_scene_begin (called from scene_reset right before sceGxmBeginScene, for framebuffer objects and for the display) sets it for such a scene when the scissor
test is off, and the first update_scissor_test of the scene leaves the quad out. Every unloaded scene sets the value explicitly (set or clear), so a surface that had it set is
clear again when the scissor is on or the switch is off. vglSetMaskBackground(mode): 0 (default) draws every quad; bit 0 framebuffer-object scenes; bit 1 the display's scene.
vglGetMaskBackgroundStats: scenes begun that way, quads left out. Host test: renderer/tests/run_vitagl_maskkeep_test.sh (model of the mask bit with a background value).

